        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "994780cf-77f9-3c96-aca0-54b0a80d667c",
                "word": "spécieux",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "113d55cc-d83f-4c56-a5ac-a21b9f8258fc",
                        "entry_id": "994780cf-77f9-3c96-aca0-54b0a80d667c",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "spécieuse"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "12c6630e-fd3b-474e-825f-5d4a016fcc43",
                        "entry_id": "994780cf-77f9-3c96-aca0-54b0a80d667c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "spécieuses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0f4f4a35-c928-3805-a05c-3e8e4e4ce908",
                        "entry_id": "994780cf-77f9-3c96-aca0-54b0a80d667c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a une apparence de vérité et de justice, mais qui n’en a, effectivement, que l’apparence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "65814ecd-304c-4b52-9aac-fb79149f97f2",
                                "sense_id": "0f4f4a35-c928-3805-a05c-3e8e4e4ce908",
                                "text": "Cette race d’hommes d’État qui semble enfin s’éteindre, malgré sa science des apparences et une certaine spécieuse régularité de mœurs, n’est au moral que la dernière écume oubliée dans le monde moderne par le monde du régent et du duc d’Orléans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4370b98-fb39-401f-b051-2801d928dac7",
                                "sense_id": "0f4f4a35-c928-3805-a05c-3e8e4e4ce908",
                                "text": "Le soir tombait, un soir équivoque d’automne :\nLes belles, se pendant rêveuses à nos bras,\nDirent alors des mots si spécieux, tout bas,\nQue notre âme depuis ce temps tremble et s’étonne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3785ef95-4576-4d31-bfe4-6c0b3eceea1e",
                                "sense_id": "0f4f4a35-c928-3805-a05c-3e8e4e4ce908",
                                "text": "Il faut rappeler qu’un savant bibliothécaire d’Agen, Jean-Baptiste Pérès, démontra, en 1817, d’une façon très spécieuse, que Napoléon n’avait jamais existé et que l’histoire de ce prétendu grand capitaine n’était qu’un mythe solaire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93e073a1-b13f-451e-8586-a977bd447139",
                                "sense_id": "0f4f4a35-c928-3805-a05c-3e8e4e4ce908",
                                "text": "Parfois je doute s’il est d’autre vertu que d’aimer, d’aimer le plus possible et toujours plus… Mais certains jours, hélas ! la vertu ne m’apparaît plus que comme une résistance à l’amour. Eh quoi ! oserais-je appeler vertu le plus naturel penchant de mon cœur ! O sophisme attrayant ! invitation spécieuse ! mirage insidieux du bonheur !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0dbd1cf-a17b-40a2-8fdb-f08eaa0bae86",
                                "sense_id": "0f4f4a35-c928-3805-a05c-3e8e4e4ce908",
                                "text": "- […] Mais regardez ma femme et vous verrez comme l’amour rend mince.\nL’argument était spécieux, Énide avait toujours été la gracilité même."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bb77bf81-8c83-4710-bc3b-a329244d1ed9",
                        "source_entry_id": "994780cf-77f9-3c96-aca0-54b0a80d667c",
                        "source_sense_id": "0f4f4a35-c928-3805-a05c-3e8e4e4ce908",
                        "target_lang_word": "specious",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "specious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a190977a-f1ba-3b78-b8b4-38608c97a224",
                                        "entry_id": "d6335fba-17dd-38ed-a830-53a07e344494",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Seemingly well-reasoned, plausible or true, but actually fallacious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "000f4c87-21f7-489f-99c5-4b050f16120f",
                                                "sense_id": "a190977a-f1ba-3b78-b8b4-38608c97a224",
                                                "text": "This idea that we must see through what we have started is specious, however good it may sound."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d861536d-bf49-40d5-bc42-d296e42dee01",
                                                "sense_id": "a190977a-f1ba-3b78-b8b4-38608c97a224",
                                                "text": "now to the discourse itself, voluble enough, and full of sentence, but that, for the most part, either specious rather than solid, or to his cause nothing pertinent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cfb3654-467b-440c-a880-d73f203a869f",
                                                "sense_id": "a190977a-f1ba-3b78-b8b4-38608c97a224",
                                                "text": "I have frequently amused myself both in public and private companies, with silently remarking, the specious errors of those who speak without reflecting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a359d150-4c02-4d37-99e1-489bb52a8748",
                                                "sense_id": "a190977a-f1ba-3b78-b8b4-38608c97a224",
                                                "text": "“Number two is that for reasons which I regarded at the time as specious and insulting, the Americans objected to your husband's presence on that committee not three weeks after it met, and asked me to replace him with somebody more to their liking. Since Magnus was kingpin of the Czecho operation and of several other little shows in Eastern Europe besides, this was a totally unrealistic demand.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c64ae10e-7442-4fcf-929c-babbe32b196d",
                                                "sense_id": "a190977a-f1ba-3b78-b8b4-38608c97a224",
                                                "text": "Feig’s Ghostbusters isn’t out until July 15, but since the project was announced in 2014 as a reboot of the hit 1984 film[…] a vocal minority of movie fans have come up with specious reasons to criticize it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1a729f9-fd2f-3d6c-9a7d-f5a50a2b87f7",
                                        "entry_id": "d6335fba-17dd-38ed-a830-53a07e344494",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Employing fallacious but deceptively plausible arguments; deceitful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f7a53d2-cdbf-46b1-863c-6e11a05ff4b3",
                                                "sense_id": "f1a729f9-fd2f-3d6c-9a7d-f5a50a2b87f7",
                                                "text": "With early virtues plant your breaſt, / The ſpecious arts of vice deteſt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14b2db56-d610-48dc-901d-6a79f8f5e078",
                                                "sense_id": "f1a729f9-fd2f-3d6c-9a7d-f5a50a2b87f7",
                                                "text": "But a third cause of the delusion is, that the Church of Rome has become more specious and deceitful than before the Reformation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc866c6c-07a9-3c9a-9bc7-5b852628286e",
                                        "entry_id": "d6335fba-17dd-38ed-a830-53a07e344494",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having an attractive appearance intended to generate a favorable response; deceptively attractive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bbc3201-2198-49d2-a914-99e983e16c06",
                                                "sense_id": "cc866c6c-07a9-3c9a-9bc7-5b852628286e",
                                                "text": "And could any thing be more ſpecious, or more equal, than that fair diſtribution of power and profit, which men called the NEW MODEL?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2641edd8-4027-454c-b1ad-d574111d9a4a",
                                                "sense_id": "cc866c6c-07a9-3c9a-9bc7-5b852628286e",
                                                "text": "[T]he success of Trajan, however transient, was rapid and specious. The degenerate Parthians, broken by intestine discord, fled before his arms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ddc002f-16e2-4b6a-b0fb-0dd174dcf794",
                                                "sense_id": "cc866c6c-07a9-3c9a-9bc7-5b852628286e",
                                                "text": "This argument, though specious, will not, upon examination, be found solid."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aaecd0f2-c2f3-34de-a03b-e791b72ef544",
                                        "entry_id": "d6335fba-17dd-38ed-a830-53a07e344494",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Beautiful, pleasing to look at."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "specious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe3660f1-e9c8-35db-ae8f-061d9e8de291",
                                        "entry_id": "c6ced16a-bab0-3dc0-bbd8-6af2457001e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of speciose (“rich in species”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
